Z||000001||batboy||10-26-1999||08:26 PM||||GM might have one, you never know. I've seen a number of those repair connectors that you splice in at well equipped auto parts stores before (like at Advanced).||||reg||1
Z||000002||mwbackus||10-27-1999||07:06 AM||||WEATHERPROOF ELECTRICAL CONNECTORS<BR>ACCEL’s Weatherproof Connectors provide OEM grade connections for do-it-yourself harness construction. Each package includes a male and female connector housing with the corresponding number of wire seals and terminals.<P>1 Pin  . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . 74811<BR>2 Pin  . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . 74812<BR>3 Pin  . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . 74813<BR>4 Pin  . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . 74814<BR>5 Pin  . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . 74815<BR>6 Pin  . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . 74816<P>  <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=117376&a=859849&p=13078852&Sequence=2">  <P>MSD also has these connectors, and I believe they may also be less expensive then the Accel's.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.msdignition.com/1ignacc.htm#anchor269663" TARGET=_blank>http://www.msdignition.com/1ignacc.htm#anchor269663</A> <P>Mike<p>[This message has been edited by mwbackus (edited 10-27-1999).]||||reg||1
